Human evaluation is performed by 3 annotators who independently score the results of 300 test queries based on the following criteria: 
(1) Good (3 points) - grammatical, semantically relevant, informative, and interesting; 
(2) Acceptable (2 points) - grammatical, semantically relevant, but too trivial or generic; 
(3) Failed (1 point) - has grammar mistakes or is irrelevant to the query.

